  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the African Union Human Rights Observers and Military Experts Mission in Burundi &#xbf; Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The action provides financial support from the African Peace Facility (APF) to the second phase of the &apos;&apos;African Union Human Rights Observers and Military Experts Mission in Burundi&apos;&apos; for the period 1 February 2019 to 31 January 2021. The main specific objectives of the operation are to: SO1: Awareness of the Human Rights and security situation in Burundi is raised among the AU, the EU and other relevant partners; SO2: Protection of victims of Human Rights violations is ensured. The expected results of the present action are the following: R 1: Violations of Human Rights, including patterns, frequency and responsibilities are observed, monitored, documented and reported; R 2: The overall security situation is monitored and reported on; R 3: Protection measures for individuals at risk and victims of Human Rights violations are provided; R 4: Accountability for Human Rights violations through judicial means is enhanced; R 5: Regular coordination and synergies with relevant national and international partners are enhanced and maintained.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
